{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/831505-looking-for-advice-on-creating-cities-campaigns","id":831505,"title":"Looking for advice on creating cities & campaigns!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-16T22:12:36-08:00","id":831505,"title":"Looking for advice on creating cities & campaigns!","content":"I'm putting together a game and while I'm fairly happy with my progress, this is the first big city setting I've done, so I wanted to straw poll the forum. When you're putting together a setting for a campaign, what parts of the city or setting do you personally detail out first? Which do you feel are absolutely necessary to detail out before you start playing?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T22:18:50-08:00","id":831508,"title":"","content":"If you mean designing a Domain for Requiem, I like to start with a high concept. What's going down in this city? Is it a thriving nexus of Kindred community, or a cloister, sectioned off from other vampires? Is the city an authoritarian dictatorship run by the Invictus, or a lawless jungle run by the Circle? Did the Strix strike here at some point? When will they come again? What's unique about vampires in this city? Is there another Clan? A particularly dominant bloodline? <br /> <br /> That's the kind of stuff I wonder about when I start off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T22:50:16-08:00","id":831517,"title":"","content":"I'd welcome advice for either creating a Kindred Domain, designing a city for it to play out in, or both! Anything would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T23:07:55-08:00","id":831522,"title":"","content":"Well, I like to use real cities, as there is never a shortage of interesting, crazy shit that can be used for fodder in a game.<br /> <br /> Do you have any sense of the kind of city you want? American? European? Asian? East Coast? West Coast? Very urban or more rural?<br /> <br /> It helps to have a real basic idea in your head of what's cool for your game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-16T23:29:13-08:00","id":831530,"title":"","content":"Well, as I said in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/815178-looking-for-inspiration-and-sources-of-non-combat-conflict\">this thread</a>, I'm working on a set of games in Paris set in different time periods. The one I'm currently prepping takes place in 1814, right as the end of Napoleon's reign (aside from the Hundred Days). I've got a general domain mostly sketched out, and I've targeted a few places for greater elaboration like the Palais Royal, the growing catacombs, and a couple of hospitals, but I'm still trying to figure out how to portray Napoleonic Paris and how to tie the domain I've come up into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T00:54:44-08:00","id":831571,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Here's how I've been going about creating a Munich set in the 1920's:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">- started off with a general concept of what's been happening up in the city up to the point the characters will be introduced, and a basic campaign arc (very loose, and with enough leeway for the players to go whichever direction they want to go with it)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">- researched the city, used a neighborhood map to plan out how territory is going to be carved out, who controls what, etc.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">- scoured the internet for photos to use as NPC portraits, started separating them into clans (this is a Masquerade campaign, so I didn't have to consider covenants, but I did plan out coteries... basically the same thing) and naming them, outlining NPC character concepts and goals, figuring out what positions they hold, etc, and then </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">assigning them to domains.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">- Did write-ups for each domain, including blurbs on the NPCs that control them. Added interesting locations for each domain - also with descriptions and (when possible) period-appropriate photos. These are a mix of fictional and real places of interest that would make cool meeting places, hangouts, hunting areas and backdrops for dramatic events.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">That's as far as I've completed so far. Took me almost a month, as it's very detailed and thought out.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The next step is completing the NPC portraits (also a time-consuming process, as I have a process to make them look like art, and with a consistent aesthetic), giving them stats, and then using Mr. Gone's coterie maps to outline the relationships between them.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Then, I'll write up a brief history.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">D</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">uring this entire process I'm brainstorming story seeds, so finally I'll pick a few to start with, and then the players will be set loose to breathe life into all of it, and, presumably, break it all to hell...</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/231-blitzburger","name":"Blitzburger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar231_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-17T01:59:13-08:00","id":831603,"title":"","content":"In rough order <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I pick a location, just something that feels interesting and appropriate for the game line and the players. This then leads to...</li> <li>A general concept for the domain and perhaps a mood and theme. This should not be too detailed yet. This then leads to...</li> <li>The current political situation. What covenant(s)/clan(s) are in power? What are their relationships like? This then leads to...</li> <li>Representative NPCs for the covenants/clans/districts/coteries. This should be general concepts only for now because this then leads too...</li> <li>Tying the concept, political situation and NPCs into the location's past and present. This requires some research, but I tend to slightly favour the side of &quot;stylish&quot; over &quot;factual&quot;.</li> </ol><br /> Once these steps are done, the most important work is over. I then pick a few important locations (in Requiem Elysiums especially), possible setpieces I would like to run the players through and come up with more NPCs in very broad strokes. As far as tying the concept to the domain, I think it helps when you have a central problem that most of the action revolves around, but also have some NPCs who do not care about it at all and are doing their own thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> For my upcoming Mage game, I gave the players a selection of five cities to choose from. I gave a quick overview of each location (~500 words each), how the political situation is special and what makes it unique and what the central Mystery is. After the vote, I created a more detailed overview in which I went into more detail on these things, added sections on what the Paths and Orders are like in the city. I could imagine adding a quick look at the makeup of the Consilum and Assembly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-18T13:50:44-08:00","id":832730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saibot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/831505-looking-for-advice-on-creating-cities-campaigns?p=831603#post831603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In rough order<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>I pick a location, just something that feels interesting and appropriate for the game line and the players. This then leads to...</li> <li>A general concept for the domain and perhaps a mood and theme. This should not be too detailed yet. This then leads to...</li> <li>The current political situation. What covenant(s)/clan(s) are in power? What are their relationships like? This then leads to...</li> <li>Representative NPCs for the covenants/clans/districts/coteries. This should be general concepts only for now because this then leads too...</li> <li>Tying the concept, political situation and NPCs into the location's past and present. This requires some research, but I tend to slightly favour the side of &quot;stylish&quot; over &quot;factual&quot;.</li> </ol><br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do something almost exactly like this as well.<br /> <br /> Setting<br /> Plot Concept: Bigger problem. Task I want them to complete.<br /> Important people: Who is in power in case the group runs into them or wants to be related to them in some way<br /> Major players: Who I need to have in order for problem to be solved.<br /> <br /> Perhaps this is just my experience as a story teller but everything should be open and fluid as sometimes your group doesnt go the direction you thought they would go. <br /> <br /> For example dont spend too much time creating each and every NPC in the ordo of the dracul because it might turn out that your players dont give a flying frack about them and never go speak to them other than brief mentions. <br /> <br /> Dont draw out every single detail of X building because perhaps your group suddenly only becomes interested in Y building. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-19T04:47:40-08:00","id":833156,"title":"","content":"For my write up of Rome (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\">here</a>), I used the Domains detailed in VtR 2e as a base. They are short, but not too much, give the essential plot points and a mix between the big guns and the new bloods of the setting. Using my Domain as an example, I proceeded this way:<br /> <br /> 1) Choose a city and a time period, something that screams &quot;Vampire&quot;. Well, you already did that. I live in Rome, so this was an easy choice. Don't go crazy with what happened before the beginning of your Chronicle, just the bare minimum to explain how your clans and covenants operate.<br /> 2) Choose a Mood. I went with &quot;Denial of the past&quot;: the vampires in the Domain have big baggage, and they tend to run away from it. This includes both their human lives (&quot;Mortals are unruly beasts next to us&quot;) and their Vampire history (&quot;The Camarilla wasn't that big of a thing, we did better&quot;). They lie, and lie, and lie.<br /> 3) Explain how the covenants operate, who is in charge and why, write something peculiar into the covenants of your city (especially the Carthians and the Circle). It's a good idea to decide beforehand which clan is more prominent in a covenant. It's sort of a short cut to give them a certain flair. My Lancea is full of Mekhet, so it operates behind the curtains, letting the Invictus rule in their stead.<br /> 4) What do the clans do? Do they respect their stereotypes or do they reject them? If the Nosferatu have a Necropolis, how is it? Are the Ventrue in charge or is everyone making fun of them (ok, I'm kidding here, but it's a prevalent trope in the book...)?<br /> 5) You probably have already decided who the Prince/Whatever is by now. Who else has real power? Who are the runts that will probably become somewhat important in the near future? Where could the PC find their place in the domain? I don't bother with a whole sheet. Just name, clan, covenant, age and BP. If they come into play, or if I know the PC will go after them one way or another, I write something more detailed.<br /> 6) If you know the city you're playing, don't bother too much with the locations, especially real life locations, write down just the basics. Actually, I wouldn't bother any way. Wing it. The world of your Chronicle is just different enough to explain away any inaccuracies. (&quot;There is a theater in this area!&quot; &quot;No. It burned down. Sorry.&quot;)<br /> 7) After all that, plot points tend to write themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-20T08:38:52-08:00","id":833857,"title":"","content":"Starting with a plot hook and working backwards is also an option. I set a chronicle in London because I needed a city big enough to have a ruling council instead of a Prince so that someone could divide them. I'm also not above stealing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've mined <b>Damnation City</b> extensively, and set a game in San Francisco to use the material from the second edition rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T05:14:00-08:00","id":834956,"title":"","content":"Damnation city. OneNote. Those are your main tools. <br /> Start out in broad strokes, describe a prince or covenant in two or three sentences, then work on something that is related to it. Describe that in a sentence or two,, rinse, repeat, and in time you'll see all your little puzzle pieces grow into full conspiracies, characters, and creeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}